- $x(3, 1, 0) = \text{False}$ (from Clause 5: $\neg x(3, 1, 0) \lor \text{False} \implies \neg x(3, 1, 0)$)
- $x(3, 0, 1) = \text{False}$ (from Clause 4: $\neg x(0, 1, 1) \lor \text{False} \implies \neg x(0, 1, 1)$)
- $x(0, 1, 1) = \text{False}$ (from Clause 1: $\neg x(3, 0, 0) \lor \text{False} \implies \neg x(3, 0, 0)$)
- $x(2, 0, 1) = \text{False}$ (from Clause 2: $\neg x(2, 0, 1) \lor \text{False} \implies \neg x(2, 0, 1)$)

Now check the remaining clauses with these assignments:
